## 🚀 Getting Started

### Building the Toolchain from Source

#### Prerequisites
- GCC / Clang or MSVC
- GNU Make

#### Build Commands
```bash
# Build the complete compiler toolchain (binaries placed in ./bin)
make
```

### Running ALXPCE Studio

#### Prerequisites
- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) (v18 or higher recommended)
- `npm`

#### Launching the IDE
```bash
cd pce-studio
npm install
npm start
```

#### Packaging Binaries
```bash
# For Windows
npm run make:win

# For other platforms
npm run make
```

---

## 📁 Repository Structure

```
hucnext/
├── bin/              # Compiled toolchain binaries (hucc, pceas, isolink, hulz, etc.)
├── doc/              # Detailed documentation and reference guides
├── examples/         # Sample HuC and assembly projects for PC Engine
├── include/          # Standard C/ASM header files and PCE hardware libraries
├── pce-studio/       # ALXPCE Studio Electron application source & PCEVM engine
│   ├── appData/      # Engine templates, pcevm runtime, fonts, and assets
│   └── src/          # React/Redux visual editor UI and compiler pipelines
├── src/              # Toolchain source code (HuC, HuCC, PCEAS, ISOlink, tools)
├── test/             # Automated test suite (470+ test cases)
└── tgemu/            # Lightweight PC Engine verification emulator
```

